{{>common_header this title="How to get games on iOS" description="How to get PSP games into PPSSPP on iPhone and iPad: upload ISO files over Wi-Fi, or copy them from a Mac or PC."}}

<div class="container">
    <h1>How to get games for PPSSPP on iOS</h1>

    <h2>What are they?</h2>

    <p>PSP games are games created for the Sony PlayStation Portable, or PSP for short.
        They are normally sold as either small plastic discs or as downloadable content on PSN.
        To use them with PPSSPP, we must turn them into files. An "ISO file" is a raw copy
        of a disc, which can be compressed into a "CSO", or compressed iso (or "CHD", an alternate format).
        For instructions on how to do this yourself, see the
        <a href="/docs/getting-started/dumping-games">instructions on dumping games</a>.
    </p>
    <p>PSP games that have been downloaded from PSN onto a real PSP can be copied off the PSP and played directly.</p>
    <p>There are also free <a href="/gethomebrew">demos and homebrew games</a> you can download.</p>

    <h2>How do I get them on my iPhone or iPad?</h2>

    <h3>Over Wi-Fi (easiest, no computer needed)</h3>
    <p>From PPSSPP 1.20, you can upload games from any computer, tablet or phone on the same Wi-Fi network:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>On the <b class="inapp">Games</b> tab, go to the folder where you want to put your games.</li>
        <li>Click the Upload icon (a folder with an up arrow).</li>
        <li>Open the address PPSSPP shows in a web browser on the other device, and upload your ISO files there.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>From a Mac, over USB</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Connect your iOS device (iPhone or iPad) via USB to your Mac.</li>
        <li>On your Mac, open the device in Finder. Click the <b class="inapp">Files</b> tab, then you should see PPSSPP listed.</li>
        <li>Drag your ISO files into the app. To see them, you may have to click the Refresh icon in the app, if it's running.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>After this, the ISO files will be located on the virtual "Memory Stick". Just pick them from the
        <b class="inapp">Games</b> tab (click the Home icon if you can't find the files).</p>
    <h3>From a Windows PC, over USB</h3>
    <p>Install Apple's <a href="https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9np83lwlpz9k">Apple Devices app</a>,
        connect your iPhone or iPad, and copy the ISO files into PPSSPP under <b class="inapp">Files</b>.</p>

    <p><a href="/docs/getting-started/installing-games-android#ios">More details</a>.</p>

    {{>unit}}
</div>

